    "title": "Dolphins look at variety of backs during preseason - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joey Cooke ,\n5 hours ago\nMARATHON — Replacing an entire backfield, the Marathon High School football team had five different players carry the ball during the preseason contest against North Broward Prep on Friday, Aug. 15, on the Middle Keys campus.\nMatthew Machado collected a Dolphins-high 52 yards on six carries. Steven Stotts reached the end zone on one of his 12 rushes, going for 30 total yards. Garrett Ruddy added 17 yards on 10 touches. Providing 24 yards on eight totes was Jesus Gonzalez. Izzy Gonzales went for 21 yards on a pair of runs.\nHowever, those 144 yards as a team were not enough to maintain against the Eagles, which scored 28 unanswered points in the first half before cruising to a 42-7 victory.\nDespite the lopsided loss, the game does not hurt the Dolphins in the FHSAA rankings as a preseason matchup.",
